# Money strategy — alex (ON)

Made on 2026-10-18. *Education and arithmetic on your own data, not personal financial advice. This assistant is not a licensed financial advisor. Check facts marked 'estimate' before you act.*

## Net total: $77,552

Everything you have minus everything you owe. Higher is better. Every option below is ranked by what it adds to this number, inside your boundaries.

- Trend: first point saved today. The change shows after 30 days.

| Part | CAD |
|---|---|
| Cash | $73,447 |
| Investments | $2,527 |
| Crypto | $1,578 |
| **Net total** | **$77,552** |

<details><summary>Each source</summary>

| Source | Part | CAD | Oldest reading |
|---|---|---|---|
| Bank accounts | cash | $71,600 | 2026-10-02 |
| Etrade TFSA | investment | $5 | <NOW> |
| Kraken BTC | crypto | $1,578 | 2026-10-16 |
| Kraken CAD | cash | $12 | 2026-10-16 |
| Wealthsimple Non-registered | investment | $14 | <NOW> |
| Wealthsimple RRSP | investment | $2,501 | <NOW> |
| Wealthsimple TFSA | investment | $7 | <NOW> |
| Wise CAD | cash | $75 | 2026-10-17 |
| Wise USD | cash | $1,760 | 2026-10-17 |

</details>
- Not counted yet: Kraken ZZCANARY: no CAD price.

### Your boundaries

- Work: at most 45 hours a week (now: unknown).
- Cash floor: $9,800 + 5 % margin, from your reserve (emergency fund + float).
- Risk: at most growth.
- New debt: at most $0.
- Home: kept, never sold.
- Change them in `[boundaries]` of your profile.toml.

### Options, best first

Each option's net total is a long-run planning estimate, not a forecast; investing can lose money. Education and arithmetic on your own data, not personal financial advice.

| # | Option | Net total a year | From |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Pay each spending category with the card the cash-back section names | +$194 | cashback |
| 2 | Keep the $63,647 above your reserve safe, at the best rate (needed in about 10 months) (range $60 to $120 a year; long-run, not a forecast) | +$90 | invest_plan |

## Cash back: where to pay

| Spending | Per year | Card (in order) | Net rate |
|---|---|---|---|
| rent | $36,000.00 | Test Grocery 4% ($24,040.00) → Test Flat 2% ($11,960.00) | 2.50% / 0.50% |
| other | $28,440.00 | Test Flat 2% | 2% |
| recurring | $960.00 | Test Grocery 4% | 4% |

- Gross cash back: **$1,808.00** a year (2.76% of card-eligible spend).
- Card fees not rebated: $150.00. Rent service fees: $540.00. Memberships: $150.00.
- **Net: $968.00 a year.**
- Rent rule (count charges, no math): Test Grocery 4% × 8 → Test Flat 2% × 4 per cap year, starting at each card's cap reset.

## Bank accounts: hold the minimum or pay the fee

Cash is valued at 2% a year (set by `goals.cash_rate`). Holding a minimum costs that rate minus what the account pays.

| Account | Fee/month | Minimum | Keep | Interest | Holding costs | Fee + rebate lost | Break-even | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Test Bank Package | $30.95 | $6,000.00 | $6,500.00 | 0% | $120.00 | $491.40 | 8.19% | hold the minimum |

- Cash held at bank minimums: $6,500.00 (counts toward the emergency fund).
- Minimums are usually the balance at the end of **every** day; one day below means the full monthly fee.
- Money moves in before it moves out: transfer first, then pay the card the same day.

## Credit score: statement targets and pay-down dates

| Card | Limit | Target at close | Keep balance under (9%) | Usual use if not paid early | Pay down by |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Test Flat 2% | $25,000.00 | $750.00 (3%) | $2,250.00 | 13.47% | Oct 23 (closes Oct 24) |
| Test Grocery 4% | $15,000.00 | $450.00 (3%) | $1,350.00 | 13.89% | Oct 23 (closes Oct 25) |
| Test Costly | $5,000.00 | $50.00 (1%) | $450.00 | 0% | Oct 16 (closes Oct 18) |

- Combined: $1,250.00 reported on $45,000.00 of limits (2.78%).
- Every card autopays its **full statement balance** from a chequing account: no interest, perfect history.
- Never close an old card; product-change it to a no-fee version to keep its age and limit.
- Mortgage in about 10 months: no new credit or hard pulls from now; pull both bureau reports 3 months before and dispute errors.

## Tax: rates and moves

- Estimated 2026 income tax on $120,000.00: $27,852.76 (average 23.21%, marginal **43.41%**).
- Capital gains: half is taxable, so a $1,000 gain costs about $217.05.
